    <item rdf:about="https://alephnull.com/w/recipes/einkorn_chocolate_chip_cookies?rev=1730553350&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2024-11-02T09:15:50-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>faith (faith@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:einkorn_chocolate_chip_cookies - created</title>
        <link>https://alephnull.com/w/recipes/einkorn_chocolate_chip_cookies?rev=1730553350&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Einkorn Chocolate Chip Cookies

From Live Simply

Ingredients

	*  8 TB (= 1 stick) unsalted butter, room temp
	*  1/2 cup brown sugar, packed
	*  1/4 cup granulated sugar
	*  2 eggs
	*  1 1/2 tsp vanilla extract
	*  2 1/2 cups einkorn flour
	*  1 tsp salt
	*  1/2 tsp baking soda</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://alephnull.com/w/recipes/chocolate_chip_cookies?rev=1730553156&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2024-11-02T09:12:36-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>faith (faith@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:chocolate_chip_cookies</title>
        <link>https://alephnull.com/w/recipes/chocolate_chip_cookies?rev=1730553156&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Chocolate Chip Cookies (Reconstructed)

When I was a kid, we used to make Toll House Cookies, but with a variation of the recipe that was then on the back of each package of Toll House chocolate chips.  I was never able to find that recipe, but this is a close reconstruction.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://alephnull.com/w/recipes/el_s_chocolate_chip_cookies?rev=1730552819&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2024-11-02T09:06:59-0400</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>faith (faith@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>recipes:el_s_chocolate_chip_cookies - [Preparation] </title>
        <link>https://alephnull.com/w/recipes/el_s_chocolate_chip_cookies?rev=1730552819&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>El's Chocolate Chip Cookies

This is the closest recipe I've found that produces the same thick Toll House Cookies I remember as child.

Ingredients

	*  1/2 cup unsalted butter
	*  1/2 cup brown sugar
	*  1/4 cup granulated sugar
	*  1 tsp vanilla
	*</description>
    </item>
